Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Natural datatypes for JSON values of RML-Core mappings
 only

A literal reference whose value looked like an integer was typed
xsd:integer for JSON and XML sources alike, in mappings of any vocabulary.
RML-Core gives a natural datatype to JSON numbers in mappings of the W3C
KG-Construct CG; an XML value is a string (kg-construct/rml-io RMLSTC0007c-d),
and the legacy RML test cases expect simple literals (RMLTC0002a, 0007c-f,
0008a-b, 0011b, 0012a in JSON and XML, RMLio/rml-test-cases).

The JSON typing now applies with new_formulation only, and XML values are no
longer typed. Test: tests/test_natural_datatypes.py.
